    <h2>SHOULD I CHOOSE GAF OR OWENS CORNING FOR MY ROOF?</h2>

    <p>If you're looking for a definitive answer, there honestly isn't one, since both brands hold up exceptionally well in the Tampa Bay area. Generally speaking, the most important question is who's doing the installation. A well-installed roof from either brand will almost always outperform a poorly installed one from the "better" manufacturer. <a href="/blog/5-questions-to-ask-your-roofer">Choose your contractor</a> at least as carefully as you choose your shingle brand.</p>

    <h2>WHY TRUST HAPPY ROOF?</h2>

    <p>Happy Roof installs both GAF and Owens Corning shingles regularly, so we have real-world experience with how each performs on Tampa Bay roofs specifically. We're an <strong>Owens Corning Preferred Contractor</strong>, which means we can offer Owens Corning's Preferred Protection workmanship warranty when you choose an OC shingle system. For GAF installations we install the full accessory system under GAF's standard lifetime limited material warranty.</p>

    <p>We're licensed, fully insured, and back every installation with an up to 15-year written workmanship warranty from Happy Roof, regardless of which shingle brand you choose. You can also use our <a href="/assessment?tab=viz">roof visualizer tool</a> to see what different shingle colors look like on your home if you're not quite sure which direction to go in yet.</p>

